+## TurboQuant KV types (`turbo3` / `turbo4`)
+
+KVMem can run its KV tier on the TurboQuant cache types. Three things had to
+line up, and only one of them was actually about kernels:
+
+1. **Flag parsing** — `kvmem_parse_cache_type()` (`tools/kvmem/kvmem-spec.cpp`)
+   now accepts `turbo3` / `turbo3_0` / `turbo4` / `turbo4_0`, and
+   `kvmem_cache_types_ok()` whitelists both types. `--kv-dtype`, `-ctk` and
+   `-ctv` advertise them; the rejection message lists them too.
+2. **Host-side codec** — nothing to do. `kvmem_cache_unpack_rows()` falls through
+   to `ggml_get_type_traits(ty)->to_float`, and `ggml.c` routes
+   `GGML_TYPE_TURBO3_0/4_0` to `quantize_turbo3_0` / `dequantize_row_turbo3_0`.
+3. **Device stage-in codec** — `src/adapter/llama-kvmem-stagein.cu`.
+
+The structural point that makes this cheap: **the tiered store is type-opaque**.
+GPU cache rows move as per-row byte copies — `RawKvStore::copy_k_gpu` →
+`kvmem_stagein_enqueue_v` / `kvmem_stagein_h2d_bytes` — inside a row already sized
+by `ggml_row_size(type, n_embd)`. Nothing in `kvmem/` or the adapter interprets
+those bytes. So turbo3/turbo4 rows round-trip through the tier with no codec at
+all, and `read_gpu_block` / `dump_kv_compare` decode through the ggml trait.
+
+The codec added to `llama-kvmem-stagein.cu` serves the *other* stage-in shape
+(`kvmem_stagein_enqueue_k`), which rebuilds a row from values: dequantise to f32
+→ RoPE → KVMem's Hadamard → re-quantise. For turbo types that last step has to
+reproduce ggml's `k_set_rows_turbo3` / `k_set_rows_turbo4` byte-for-byte,
+otherwise a rebuilt row would not match the rows prefill wrote natively into the
+same cache.
+
+| Added | Notes |
+|---|---|
+| `dequant_turbo3` / `dequant_turbo4` | centroid × block norm, matching `dequantize_row_turbo3_0` / `_turbo4_0` |
+| `quant_turbo3_grouped<128\|64>` | group L2 norm → signed FWHT → nearest centroid → pack 2+1 bits → reconstruction-corrected norm |
+| `quant_turbo4_grouped` | same, one 128-element block, nibble packing, `rnorm` written as 0 |
+| `kvmem_stagein_quant_ok` | widened to the two turbo types |
+
+Two deliberate deviations from `set-rows.cu`:
+
+- **No `__shfl_*`, no `__ballot_*`.** HIP's wavefront is 64 on GCN and 32 on RDNA
+  and this tree targets gfx1030, so every reduction is a shared-memory tree and
+  the sub-block packing is addressed in shared memory. The result does not depend
+  on wavefront size.
+- **The WHT group size comes from `head_dim`, not the row width** —
+  `(n_embd_head % 128 == 0) ? 128 : 64`, mirroring the `op_params` written by
+  `llama-kv-cache.cpp:1415`. For head_dim 128 (the 27B case) the two rules agree;
+  they differ only for head_dim 64 with an even KV head count, where the
+  row-width rule would merge two heads into one group.
+
+`tools/kvmem/gen-turbo-tables.py` generates
+`src/adapter/llama-kvmem-turbo-{host,device}.h` from
+`ggml/src/ggml-cuda/turbo-quant.cuh`, so the codebooks and the WHT sign tables
+cannot drift from ggml's. `--check` asserts the generated files are current.
+
+Verified on `llama-kvmem-server.exe`:
+
+| Check | Result |
+|---|---|
+| `--kv-dtype turbo3 -ctk turbo3 -ctv turbo4` | accepted, then `KVMEM_STARTUP_ERROR missing model` |
+| `--kv-dtype turbo3_0` | accepted (alias) |
+| `--kv-dtype turbo9` | `unsupported cache type (want f16\|f32\|q8_0\|q5_0\|q4_0\|turbo3\|turbo4)` |
