+
+### What is *not* proven
+
+The device codec compiled but never ran. This sandbox has no ROCm device, and
+`kvmem_stagein_enqueue_k` currently has **no caller**: the live stage-in is
+`write_block_to_gpu()`, which copies raw rows through `kvmem_stagein_enqueue_v` /
+`kvmem_stagein_h2d_bytes`. So the turbo kernels are compile-verified only, and
+what actually carries turbo3/turbo4 at runtime is the type-opaque byte path.
+
+First real check, on the user's own terminal:
+
+```bash
+llama-kvmem-server -m <head_dim-128 model> --kv-dtype turbo3 -ngl 99
+```
+
+A head_dim-128 model is required: `llama-kv-cache.cpp:214-233` silently falls the
+cache back to `q8_0` (with a warning on layer 0) if turbo3 gets head_dim % 64,
+or turbo4 head_dim % 128.
